zig-ozz-animation is a clean Zig port derived from the design and binary
formats of ozz-animation 0.16:

  https://github.com/guillaumeblanc/ozz-animation
  Copyright (c) Guillaume Blanc
  Licensed under the MIT License.

The math facade uses Caliper:

  https://github.com/flying-swallow/caliper
  Copyright (c) its contributors
  Licensed under the MIT License.

The glTF importer uses flying-swallow/zgltf:

  https://github.com/flying-swallow/zgltf
  Copyright (c) 2022 Alexandre Chêne
  Licensed under the MIT License.

The standalone benchmark package uses zBench:

  https://github.com/hendriknielaender/zBench
  Copyright (c) its contributors
  Licensed under the MIT License.

The standalone desktop samples use rhi-zig:

  https://github.com/flying-swallow/rhi-zig
  Copyright (c) Michael Pollind
  Licensed under GPL-2.0-only.

They use SDL:

  https://github.com/castholm/SDL
  Copyright (c) Sam Lantinga and SDL contributors
  Licensed under the zlib License.

No rhi-zig code is linked into the MIT-licensed core or command-line tool.
